    "narrative": "The core of today\u2019s offensive attack centers on **Corbin Carroll** (71.87) and **Mickey Moniak** (71.22), who present our highest efficiency ceilings. **Corbin Carroll** remains a priority start; despite a slight platoon dip against Wrobleski, his aggressive base-stealing potential is unlocked by the pitcher's slow delivery, a critical factor in our strategy to capture the scarce SB category. **Mickey Moniak** benefits from a strong platoon advantage against McGreevy, with his 14% boost driving him into the elite tier. Meanwhile, **Isaac Paredes** (68.21) provides the most reliable internal metrics of the day, as he draws a highly favorable matchup against the hittable V\u00e1squez, whose 4.97 xERA allows for a significant 19% SP skill boost to **Isaac Paredes**'s baseline projection.\n\nWe face a difficult decision at the edges of the roster, where **Cole Young** (40.82) just missed the cut. While **Cole Young** benefits from a strong spot in the batting order and potential SB opportunities against Seymour, his overall offensive efficiency was edged out by the superior matchup context afforded to **Brice Turang** and **Gabriel Moreno**. We are monitoring risk factors across the board, specifically for **Austin Riley** (43.54), who faces the toughest arm of the day in Schlittler (2.91 xERA). While **Austin Riley** avoids the bench, his viability is heavily capped by the elite opposing pitching; similarly, **Josh Naylor** (43.69) is forced to contend with Seymour's strong skill set, leaving both players in \"marginal\" start territory. We will continue to avoid the volatility associated with **Zach McKinstry**, who remains sidelined by our 40-point floor threshold due to his late-order placement and unfavorable platoon outlook.",
